From: PiSight development <pisight@local>
Subject: [PATCH] base: log: skip suppressed message construction and operands

The default INFO threshold currently discards DEBUG messages only after
formatting them, including prefixes and expensive stream operands. Check the
category level before construction. Keep Fatal unconditional and retain
namespace-qualified calls, Loggable prefixes, stream manipulators, and
single-statement if/else use. Enabled messages retain the existing logger.
Two static methods explicitly select the namespace logger: qualifying LOG alone
now qualifies its guard, not its final backend expression. LOG has void type;
its internal documentation reflects this statement-style, lazy contract.

--- a/include/libcamera/base/log.h
+++ b/include/libcamera/base/log.h
@@ -105,12 +105,30 @@
 		const char *fileName = __builtin_FILE(),
 		unsigned int line = __builtin_LINE());
 
+/* Avoid constructing messages, prefixes or stream operands below the level. */
+inline bool _logShouldSkip(const LogCategory *category, LogSeverity severity)
+{
+	if (severity == LogFatal)
+		return false;
+
+	return severity < (category ? *category : LogCategory::defaultCategory()).severity();
+}
+
+class LogMessageVoidify
+{
+public:
+	void operator&(std::ostream &) const {}
+};
+
 #ifndef __DOXYGEN__
 #define _LOG_CATEGORY(name) logCategory##name
 
 #define _LOG1(severity) \
-	_log(nullptr, Log##severity).stream()
+	_logShouldSkip(nullptr, Log##severity) ? static_cast<void>(0) : \
+	::libcamera::LogMessageVoidify() & _log(nullptr, Log##severity).stream()
 #define _LOG2(category, severity) \
+	_logShouldSkip(&_LOG_CATEGORY(category)(), Log##severity) ? static_cast<void>(0) : \
+	::libcamera::LogMessageVoidify() & \
 	_log(&_LOG_CATEGORY(category)(), Log##severity).stream()
 
 /*
--- a/src/libcamera/base/log.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/base/log.cpp
@@ -1014,10 +1014,11 @@
  * \param[in] category Category (optional)
  * \param[in] severity Severity
  *
- * Return an std::ostream reference to which a message can be logged using the
- * iostream API. The \a category, if specified, sets the message category. When
- * absent the default category is used. The  \a severity controls whether the
- * message is printed or discarded, depending on the log level for the category.
+ * Log a message using the iostream insertion syntax as a statement. The
+ * expression has void type. The \a category, if specified, sets the message
+ * category; otherwise the default category is used. Messages below the category
+ * level skip construction and do not evaluate stream operands or object prefixes.
+ * Do not rely on side effects in stream operands.
  *
  * If the severity is set to Fatal, execution is aborted and the program
  * terminates immediately after printing the message.
